# Executable scripts must keep LF. A CRLF checkout (core.autocrlf=true on
# Windows) leaves a carriage return on the shebang line, which Node tolerates
# but esbuild — and therefore vitest, when a spec imports one of these — rejects
# with "SyntaxError: Invalid or unexpected token".
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.mts text eol=lf
*.sh  text eol=lf
